# IMPORTANT: Vite requires all frontend environment variables to start with the "VITE_" prefix!
# This allows Vite to automatically inject them securely during the build phase.

# Local Development Fallback:
# If this file is empty or not present locally, the code natively falls back to '' 
# which seamlessly catches into the proxy loop designed in vite.config.js
# VITE_API_URL=""

# Production Example (Azure VM Context):
# During your actual Azure Static Web Apps build deployment, 
# you should set this environment variable in the Azure Portal Settings to your deployed backend's public IP!
VITE_API_URL=http://your-azure-vm-ip-here:8000
